        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Menstrual history and bleeding"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports regular cycles every 28–30 days, bleeding for 6–7 days, with heavy bleeding during the first 2–3 days. Uses super pads, changing every 2–3 hours on heavy days; occasional small clots. No flooding through clothes and no nocturnal sheet soaking. Bleeding may be a bit heavier this year but remains manageable and has not caused missed work."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Pelvic symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports some pelvic fullness, especially around her period, with no constant pain. Mild dysmenorrhoea on days 1–2. Denies dyspareunia, dysuria, change in bowel habit, increased urinary frequency or urgency."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported associated symptoms and vaginal symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies intermenstrual bleeding, postcoital bleeding, abnormal vaginal discharge, fever, night sweats, weight loss, shortness of breath, unusual exertional fatigue, and dizziness. Reports no known history of anaemia."
      }
    },
    {
